# Local-only, interactive Moodle/Playwright automation — not part of the
# deployed API. moodle/sync_service.py (used by POST /api/sync/moodle) and
# moodle/document_downloader.py (its sync_resource_documents() is called
# from sync_service.py's run_sync() — see BUILD_LOG.md) are NOT excluded.
#
# moodle/browser.py is NOT excluded either, as of the multi-user
# foundation work (see BUILD_LOG.md) — this used to be true ("never
# imported at module level ... specifically so its absence here is
# safe") but is no longer: moodle/sync_service.py's run_sync() now does
# `from moodle.browser import check_moodle_session` (a real, reachable
# runtime import whenever a sync is triggered with a user_id — i.e.
# every multi-user sync), and api/routes.py's POST /api/moodle/connect
# and GET /api/moodle/session-status import check_moodle_session /
# connect_user_interactively from it too. Excluding it here previously
# built a container image that raised `ModuleNotFoundError: No module
# named 'moodle.browser'` the first time any of those code paths
# actually ran on Render — confirmed as the real, reproduced root cause
# (see BUILD_LOG.md's deployment-fix entry), not a hypothetical. Its own
# interactive-only entry points (main(), get_authenticated_page(), both
# gated behind a blocking input() prompt) are simply never called by the
# deployed API and sit unused — importing the module at all does not
# execute them.
moodle/browser_profile/
moodle/__pycache__/
content_radar.py
course_radar.py
submission_radar.py
voice.py
browser_profile/
state/

# Local persistent data — not baked into the image; production data
# lives under ESMERELDA_DATA_DIR (see storage/paths.py) instead.
storage/esmerelda.db
storage/documents/
